      // hair over the horizon, the longest and haziest path in the
      // atmosphere. Every far pixel of a bay then reflected that single colour
      // and the water from the horizon half-way down the frame went a flat
      // mustard band at golden hour (reported on the Golden Gate from Baker
      // Beach). Real water there is a sheet of facets tilted toward the eye,
      // each reflecting sky some way up, so the mirror direction is raised by
      // the rms slope the faded octaves were carrying (waveAlpha, the same
      // number the glint's GGX lobe uses).
